  "annotations": [
    {
      "decisionIndex": 1,
      "player": "G54m Proud",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The 7-card hand has two lands and a smooth curve of castable artifacts (all colorless). Locthwain Gargoyle on T1, Runed Servitor or Alchemist's Vial on T2 (Vial draws a card to find land 3), Thaumaturge's Familiar on T3 (scries to find more lands). While only 2 lands is slightly risky, the hand functions well and has built-in card selection.",
      "actionTaken": "Mulliganed to 6 cards",
      "betterLine": "Keep the 7-card hand. It has a functional curve with all colorless spells matching the colorless mana base, and Alchemist's Vial + Thaumaturge's Familiar provide card selection to find the third land.",
      "snapshotIndex": 3,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 3,
      "player": "G54m Proud",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Bottomed Alchemist's Vial, which is the only artifact in hand and the key synergy piece for Skilled Animator. Without an artifact to animate, Skilled Animator becomes a mediocre 1/3. The Vial also cantrips on entry, making it a strong card in its own right. Meanwhile, the Urza lands (Mine and Tower) without Power-Plant are strictly worse than basic lands.",
      "actionTaken": "Bottomed Alchemist's Vial",
      "betterLine": "Bottom Urza's Mine or Urza's Tower (they're just colorless-producing lands without the third Tron piece) and keep Alchemist's Vial to enable the Skilled Animator synergy (turn 3 Vial + draw, turn 4 Animator = 5/5 artifact creature).",
      "snapshotIndex": 4,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 34,
      "player": "G54m Proud",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Discarding Island when they only have 3 lands on board (and 0 land drops remaining this turn but will need lands in future turns). With Skilled Animator costing 2U and only one Island for blue mana, keeping the Island for a future land drop could be more valuable than keeping Golem Artisan, which costs 5 and won't be castable for several turns.",
      "actionTaken": "Discarded Island",
      "betterLine": "Discard Golem Artisan - it's the most expensive card at 5 mana and won't be castable for many turns. Keeping the Island ensures future blue mana for Skilled Animator and Aether Spellbomb's bounce ability.",
      "snapshotIndex": 43,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 35,
      "player": "G54m Proud",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "The game engine listed Aether Spellbomb as a legal cast option, meaning mana was available to cast it. Having Aether Spellbomb on the battlefield is valuable both for its utility (bounce/draw) and critically as a target for Skilled Animator next turn, which would turn it into a 5/5 artifact creature. Passing here wastes the opportunity to deploy a cheap artifact that enables a powerful turn 6 play.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority without casting anything.",
      "betterLine": "Cast Aether Spellbomb to have it on the battlefield, setting up Skilled Animator next turn to animate it into a 5/5 creature.",
      "snapshotIndex": 45,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 47,
      "player": "G54m Proud",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Walking Ballista with only 3 mana available (X=1, entering as a 1/1) instead of Thaumaturge's Familiar, which would be a 1/3 flyer with scry 1 for the same mana cost. The Familiar is a superior board presence (survives Grim Lavamancer's 2-damage ability, has evasion), provides scry to find needed lands, and Walking Ballista scales much better if saved for later when more mana is available (especially if Tron is completed).",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Walking Ballista for X=1 as a 1/1",
      "betterLine": "Cast Thaumaturge's Familiar as a 1/3 flyer with scry 1, saving Walking Ballista for later when it can enter with more counters",
      "snapshotIndex": 62,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 98,
      "player": "G31FL Pessim",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Casting Magmaquake before playing the Mountain from hand. With current 5 mana (4 lands + Mana Geode), Magmaquake can only be X=3. Playing Mountain first would give 6 mana, allowing X=4. While X=3 still kills Skilled Animator (3 damage to 3 toughness) and Merfolk Pupil, X=4 provides a safety margin and is strictly better.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast Magmaquake without first playing Mountain from hand",
      "betterLine": "Play Mountain first, then cast Magmaquake with X=4 using all 6 available mana to maximize damage",
      "snapshotIndex": 123,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 102,
      "player": "G31FL Pessim",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Declined to cast Weight of Conscience when it was the only available play and would have neutralized the opponent's 5/5 Aether Spellbomb, the primary threat. G31FL is at 13 life facing a 5/5 attacker with no other removal in sight for the immediate future. Weight of Conscience would prevent the 5/5 from attacking, buying critical time.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority without casting Weight of Conscience",
      "betterLine": "Cast Weight of Conscience targeting the animated Aether Spellbomb 5/5 to prevent it from attacking, preserving life total and buying time to deploy Cinder Elemental or find other answers.",
      "snapshotIndex": 133,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 112,
      "player": "G54m Proud",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to activate Merfolk Pupil's graveyard ability ({1}{U}, exile from graveyard: draw a card, then discard a card) during combat when 3 untapped lands were available and no instant-speed plays in hand to hold mana for. This is a free card quality improvement with no cost beyond the mana that has no other use this combat.",
      "actionTaken": "Passed priority without activating Merfolk Pupil from graveyard",
      "betterLine": "Activate Merfolk Pupil from graveyard for {1}{U} to loot (draw then discard) and improve card quality, since there are no other instant-speed plays to hold mana for during combat.",
      "snapshotIndex": 149,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 119,
      "player": "G54m Proud",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarded Expedition Map, which could search for Urza's Power-Plant to complete the Tron set (Mine + Tower + Power-Plant), providing a massive mana advantage. With Tron online, the player would have access to 7+ mana from just 3 lands, enabling them to quickly deploy their expensive 5-mana threats (Gearsmith Guardian, Golem Artisan). Instead, weaker cards like Locthwain Gargoyle (a 0/3 that needs 4 mana to become a mediocre attacker) should have been discarded.",
      "actionTaken": "Discarded Expedition Map",
      "betterLine": "Discard Locthwain Gargoyle, which is the weakest card in hand. Keep Expedition Map to search for Urza's Power-Plant and complete Tron for a huge mana advantage.",
      "snapshotIndex": 157,
    },
    {
      "decisionIndex": 125,
      "player": "G31FL Pessim",
      "type": "blunder",
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Playing King of the Pride (a 2/1) doesn't address the main threat: the 5/5 animated Aether Spellbomb. At 7 life, the 5/5 is a two-turn clock. While King of the Pride + Weight of Conscience is a possible two-step plan, Volcanic Geyser (X=1) on Skilled Animator permanently removes the 5/5 threat by killing the animator, and leaves 3 mana for King of the Pride - developing the board while solving the problem more cleanly.",
      "actionTaken": "Cast King of the Pride ({2}{W})",
      "betterLine": "Cast Volcanic Geyser (X=1) targeting Skilled Animator (1/3) for 3 mana, then cast King of the Pride for remaining 3 mana. This permanently removes the 5/5 threat while still developing the board.",
